  "limitations": [
    "Pilot only: one PIE video (set01/video_0004) of one scene group; windows are strongly correlated (same scene, camera, drive and overlapping tracks). No independent train/validation/test split exists; nothing here supports a generalization claim.",
    "PILOT_SMOKE targets are perceived YOLO11n + ByteTrack positions of the same tracks; they inherit detector/tracker errors and are not independent ground truth. Phase 3 detection/tracking quality on PIE has not been measured.",
    "Image space only (captured_1920x1080 pixels, px/s, s); image velocities mix agent motion with moving-camera ego-motion and perspective.",
    "Node velocities are Task 2 one-frame (1/30 s) causal backward differences with ~48 px/s per-axis jitter; no smoothing.",
    "Bicyclist nodes come from the COCO 'bicycle' detection class (Phase 3 label 'bike' mapped to 'bicyclist' by assumption). A bicycle detection is not evidence of a rider (parked bicycles are possible). They are stored, flagged semantically_uncertain, and excluded from the default context.",
    "Strict target policy: windows need the target at all 6 history and 15 future samples; short and fragmented tracks are under-represented, which biases the pilot towards long, continuously tracked pedestrians.",
    "Track fragments and possible identity switches are not repaired or merged; Phase 3 class-flip holes remain.",
    "Overlapping windows of the same track share frames (stride 0.1 s, window span 2.0 s); the effective sample size is closer to the number of distinct tracks than to the number of windows."
  ],
